comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T18:58:31.352Z",codex-root,Live instance returns 403 for JSON while HTML search succeeds; response negotiation is mandatory.
  "2026-07-21T19:11:09.654Z",codex-root,"Live installed-command proof: raw output reported _upstreamFormat=html and five upstream engine timeouts; repeated validated JSON query produced cached=true; cache status reports unlimited and Endless. Full live E2E script passed after making zero-result format checks schema-aware."
  "2026-07-21T19:12:10.309Z",codex-root,"Quality acceptance was raised after initial coverage measurement. Current honest baseline is statements 72.70%, branches 60.81%, functions 84.48%, lines 74.67%; publication is blocked until the mandated 100/100/100/100 gate and docstring/static/security layers are real."
  "2026-07-21T19:29:56.312Z",codex-root,"Global latest reinstall reproduced pm-cli bundle_integrity_torn_install; uninstall plus exact latest reinstall restored the Homebrew-prefix binary. This matches existing unbraind/pm-cli#634, so no duplicate issue was filed."
  "2026-07-21T20:12:22.301Z",codex-root,"Installed-package E2E found and fixed cache lifecycle loss: every CLI invocation now loads the persistent cache before exit handlers can save it. Repeated real searxng processes prove firstCached=false, secondCached=true, entries=1, maxSize=unlimited, maxAge=Endless."
  "2026-07-21T20:15:12.473Z",codex-root,"Current mandatory coverage gate correctly fails at statements 72.55%, branches 60.91%, functions 84.00%, lines 74.49%. The gate remains 100% per file; no source exclusions, ignore pragmas, mocked acceptance, or threshold reductions were used."
  "2026-07-21T20:15:12.473Z",codex-root,Security sweep found MCP SDK 1.29.0 resolved @hono/node-server 1.19.14 with GHSA-frvp-7c67-39w9. Raised the explicit override to 2.0.11; bun audit is now clean and all 628 unit tests plus typechecking pass.
  "2026-07-21T20:17:43.731Z",codex-root,"After adding executable entry-point success/failure coverage and rejected-request cleanup coverage, 20 files and 631 tests pass. Honest coverage moved to statements 72.66%, branches 60.88%, functions 84.76%, lines 74.61%; the 100% per-file gate still correctly blocks release."
  "2026-07-21T21:52:02.707Z",codex-root,"End-to-end implementation verification checkpoint: full repository coverage now passes at 100/100/100/100 across 930 tests. Test matrices cover local-routing enforcement, TOON/JSON/JSONL/YAML/XML/CSV/Markdown/table/text/HTML formats, schemas and payload validation, setup-local states, cache CRUD/offline/semantic behavior, request JSON, autocomplete, presets, multi-search/strict modes, doctor and formatter verification, MCP dispatch, and the built-in acceptance suite. Proceeding to complete quality/security/live-service/package/release gates."
  "2026-07-21T22:23:19.586Z",codex-root,"PM linked-test execution was attempted in schema and tracker modes. The project pm-changelog command entered a fresh pm init prompt because extension dependency resolution is unavailable in the linked-test sandbox, matching the existing searx-changelog-migration learning. It remains a mandatory direct workspace gate; the other linked gates are executed through PM."
  "2026-07-21T22:24:08.200Z",codex-root,"The composite live release:check was also removed from PM sandbox execution because it intentionally contains the same project-owned pm-changelog gate. Direct workspace release:check already passed end-to-end against 192.168.1.183:38522; PM retains its constituent lint, coverage, build, security, package, and live E2E commands."
  "2026-07-21T22:38:04.140Z",codex-root,"Final local gate checkpoint: 20 files and 931 tests pass at 100% statements (4636/4636), branches (3389/3389), functions (521/521), and lines (4339/4339); module docstrings are 18/18. Bun audit exposed newly published GHSA-v2hh-gcrm-f6hx against fast-uri 3.1.3, so the override moved to patched 3.1.4; Bun audit, Trivy, history secret scan, quality, package smoke, changelog checks, and live release:check are green. Prettier is current at 3.9.6; TypeScript remains 6.0.3 because latest typescript-eslint requires TypeScript below 6.1."
notes[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T18:58:31.352Z",codex-root,Preserve legacy global flags while establishing explicit command-family contracts.
  "2026-07-21T19:12:11.256Z",codex-root,"New mandatory constraints: eliminate unjustified any, inline one-use trivial helpers, use top-level/static imports, preserve erasable TypeScript syntax, inspect dependency declarations instead of guessing, enforce docstring coverage, and add non-cheatable unit/integration/E2E/performance/acceptance/functional/smoke/dogfood/white-box/black-box gates."
  "2026-07-21T19:29:57.670Z",codex-root,"Operational caveat: verify the pm binary and version immediately after global upgrades; the current confirmed latest is 2026.7.21."
  "2026-07-21T20:12:22.301Z",codex-root,"The configured SearXNG instance is reachable and advertises 241 engines, 31 categories, 62 locales, and 9 plugins, but enabled upstream engines currently time out. CLI transport, HTML fallback, zero-result schema handling, formatter contracts, and error metadata are therefore the available live acceptance surface."
  "2026-07-21T20:15:12.473Z",codex-root,npm audit cannot execute in this Bun-lockfile repository because npm requires package-lock.json; bun audit and Trivy are the authoritative dependency scans and are both clean after the Hono override.
  "2026-07-21T22:22:14.417Z",codex-root,"Review governance uses scripts/pr-review-inventory.mjs to capture exact-head checks plus every conversation comment, submitted review, inline thread, resolution state, edit time, and reaction total. Human judgment remains explicit for voting, thread replies, and resolution."
learnings[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T18:58:31.352Z",codex-root,Full SearXNG compatibility must follow instance-advertised capabilities rather than assume API formats are enabled.
  "2026-07-21T20:12:22.301Z",codex-root,Persistent state must be loaded before process-wide exit persistence is armed; otherwise read-only commands can truncate state created by prior processes.
  "2026-07-21T22:22:15.059Z",codex-root,"A cache hit must not launch unref background refresh work in a one-shot CLI: open network handles delay process termination and make installed-command acceptance nondeterministic. Explicit refresh commands preserve predictable CLI lifecycle semantics."
  "2026-07-21T22:38:04.736Z",codex-root,"Security databases can disagree temporarily: Bun audit detected the fast-uri host-confusion advisory while the current Trivy database still reported zero. Release security requires both gates and remediation of the stricter result."
